@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP ProjectForge. Remove current dependency on reviews/workflow/deployment/communications; retain advanced functions as future.
title MVP ProjectForge — basic Git, issues and simple Kanban
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam wrapWidth 190
actor "Native Git client\nCommits normally created here" as CL
rectangle "Resumefolio core" as C
package "ProjectForge — separate system" {
 component "Authenticated user / repository authority" as A
 component "Native repository adapter\nEngine / transport undecided" as G
 database "Repository objects / refs\nProjectForge storage ownership" as D
 component "File/history browsing\nIssues / simple Kanban" as W
 A --> G
 G --> D
 A --> W
}
CL --> A : real clone / fetch / pull / push\nseparate native transport authority
C <--> A : authenticated user-scoped API
rectangle "AFTER MVP\nAdvanced PR / review / merge / releases\nAdvanced backlog / Sprints\nYAML execution / deployment" as X #F8EBD7
legend bottom
 No shared core database, server-created-commit promise or GitHub parity.
 ProjectForge physical deployment, engine and database remain undecided.
endlegend
@enduml
